{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Because of this YHWH did for me. Because of this that YHWH did for me when I went out of Egypt</b>. And likewise \"and you shall make known to them the way they shall walk in it\" (Exodus 18:20), and many similar. He says: because <b>of this that YHWH did for me when I went out of Egypt</b> I perform this service, in the same sense as what He says below (Exodus 13:15), \"therefore I sacrifice to YHWH every firstborn of the womb\" — and he said this, meaning you shall tell him this that you see with your own eyes that YHWH did for you when you went out of Egypt. And our Sages interpreted (in the Mekhilta here) that he hints at the matzah and maror that are placed before him. And it is possible that its division is <b>and you shall tell your son: because of this YHWH did for me when I went out of Egypt</b> — saying thus and thus did YHWH do for me, for the word בַּעֲבוּר also serves for the essence of the matter itself, as in \"because of the child living, you fasted and wept\" (II Samuel 12:21) — it is not 'on account of.' And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 13:8) that <b>because of this</b> — that I do and perform before him in eating the pesach and the matzah — <b>YHWH did</b> for me signs until He brought me out <b>of Egypt</b>, and it is not correct. And I will further explain the verse (Ramban on Exodus 13:16):"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:07:18.563112287Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}